The Gnomish Mines I visualize along these lines.  In the Dungeon of Doom,
since monsters of incompatible type blink into existence all the time, I
imagine that they're just wandering around looking for mayhem, food and/or
loot.  Same as me.  ;-)

If I explore a level completely, and then a monster comes into existence,
why would he/she/it know about the polymorph trap?

>If the monster is of below-average intelligence, I would say you have a gripe.
>Remember though, that these guys grew up around wands and potions.  Monsters'
>seemingly inate ability to identify wands and potions is just a simulated 
>reflection of their experience in the mines, or the dungeons, or whatever.
>Imagine if you had spent your whole life playing NetHack, your "identified"
>list would be pretty close to complete...

The more the conversation wanders along these lines, the more I realize that
we're running into the philosophical questions of how the monsters and items
came to be where they are, and why they're so pristine until the moment you
arrive, at which point they get tunneled and scorched and otherwise trashed.

These are probably questions best left unanswered.

